    "text": "To find the average (mean) of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using each of the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(8\\) exactly once, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the total number of such 5-digit numbers:**\n   Since we are using the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(8\\) exactly once, the total number of different 5-digit numbers is the number of permutations of these 5 digits. This is given by \\(5!\\):\n   \\[\n   5! = 5 \\times 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 120\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the contribution of each digit to the sum of all numbers:**\n   Each digit will appear in each decimal place (units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands) the same number of times. Since there are 5 digits and \\(5!\\) permutations, each digit will appear in each place \\( \\frac{120}{5} = 24 \\) times.\n\n3. **Determine the sum of the contributions of each digit in each place:**\n   - For the units place: Each digit contributes its value multiplied by 10000 (since it is in the units place). The sum of the contributions of each digit in the units place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8) \\times 10000 = 24 \\times 24 \\times 10000 = 5760000\n     \\]\n   - For the tens place: Each digit contributes its value multiplied by 1000 (since it is in the tens place). The sum of the contributions of each digit in the tens place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8) \\times 1000 = 24 \\times 24 \\times 1000 = 576000\n     \\]\n   - For the hundreds place: Each digit contributes its value multiplied by 100 (since it is in the hundreds place). The sum of the contributions of each digit in the hundreds place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8) \\times 100 = 24 \\times 24 \\times 100 = 57600\n     \\]\n   - For the thousands place: Each digit contributes its value multiplied by 10 (since it is in the thousands place). The sum of the contributions of each digit in the thousands place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8) \\times 10 = 24 \\times 24 \\times 10 = 5760\n     \\]\n   - For the ten-thousands place: Each digit contributes its value multiplied by 1 (since it is in the ten-thousands place). The sum of the contributions of each digit in the ten-thousands place is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times (1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 8) \\times 1 = 24 \\times 24 \\times 1 = 576\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total sum of all the 5-digit numbers:**\n   The total sum of all the 5-digit numbers is the sum of the contributions from each place:\n   \\[\n   5760000 + 576000 + 57600 + 5760 + 576 = 6400000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the average of all the 5-digit numbers:**\n   The average is the total sum divided by the number of such numbers:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average} = \\frac{6400000}{120} = 5333.3333\\ldots = 5333 \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the average of all 5-digit numbers that can be formed using the digits \\(1, 3, 5, 7,\\) and \\(8\\) exactly once is \\(\\boxed{5333 \\frac{1}{3}}\\).",
